              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مخدة — mikhadda — \"a cushion; a pillow\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "وضعت المخدة تحت رأسي. waḍaʿtu al-mikhadda taḥta raʾsī. I put the cushion under my head."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مخدة (mikhadda) is built on the native Arabic root kh-d-d, \"to furrow; the cheek\" (Lane). Lane gives mikhadda as a pillow, so called because it is put under the cheek, khadd, which you know."
            }
          ]
